     "how": "This is the canonical in-tree consumer and the one to fold onto the new view. It takes ONE `ps -ef` snapshot, then walks ppid depth-bounded (8) so a self-contradicting table truncates instead of spinning, and it collects descendants BEFORE killing because a kill reparents the children. Its `$2/$3 ~ /^[0-9]+$/` guard is the existing 'real process, not a fragment' rule. Lift the snapshot, the guard and the depth bound into the shared reader, then make remove_descendants call it. Keep the rule that the snapshot is deleted only AFTER the survivor re-scan.",
